# Lesson 5: Connections
# NOW the child starts combining words. Two-word phrases.
# "Cat soft." "Dog big." "Mama warm."
# These are the first triples — but they emerge from
# having already paired words with experiences.

cat is soft
cat is furry
dog is big
dog is furry
ball is round
mama is warm
dada is warm
red is bright
hot is danger
cup has water
cat has tail
dog has tail
cat has legs
dog has legs
mama has name
dada has name
